      "body": "Tuning config for Qwen3-Coder-Next (E=512,N=512 MoE dimensions, FP8 quantization) on NVIDIA RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell Server Edition. Generated using vLLM's benchmark_moe.py across 1920 kernel configurations and 15 batch sizes.\r\n\r\n## Purpose\r\nNo pre-built MoE tuning config existed for NVIDIA RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell Server Edition when running Qwen3-Coder-Next (E=512,N=512 MoE dimensions, FP8 quantization) — vLLM was falling back to default, unoptimized settings and logging \"Using default MoE config. Performance might be sub-optimal!\". This PR adds the tuning config generated for this GPU.\r\n\r\n## Test Plan\r\nRan vLLM's benchmark_moe.py with --model Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-Next-FP8, --dtype fp8_w8a8, --tp-size 1, tuning across 1920 kernel configurations for 15 different batch sizes on a real RTX PRO 6000.\r\n\r\n## Test Result\r\nGenerated config file was validated with vLLM — the model started up successfully with the new config and served requests at the expected throughput.\r\n\r\n---\r\n<details>\r\n<summary> Essential Elements of an Effective PR Description Checklist </summary>\r\n\r\n- [x] The purpose of the PR, such as \"Fix some issue (link existing issues this PR will resolve)\".\r\n- [x] The test plan, such as providing test command.\r\n- [x] The test results, such as pasting the results comparison before and after, or e2e results\r\n- [ ] (Optional) The necessary documentation update, such as updating `supported_models.md` and `examples` for a new model.\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n",
